msgid "Try it in 30 seconds"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You know the feeling. Three terminals open, a dozen services, and a wall of "
"logs scrolling past. Which one just\n"
"restarted? Was that _orders_ or _order-history_? You scroll back up, squint, "
"and hunt for the line that tells\n"
"you."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus already prints a banner at start-up -- but it is the *same* banner "
"for every application. So I built a\n"
"small Quarkiverse extension that fixes that: *Quarkus Banner* turns your "
"application name into a big, unmissable\n"
"piece of ASCII art."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Now when that service scrolls past, you know exactly what you are looking at "
"-- no squinting required."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the extension:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Start your app. That is it -- you already have a banner built from your "
"application name. Want to make it your\n"
"own? Pick some text with `quarkus.banner-generator.text` and a font with "
"`quarkus.banner-generator.font`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "246 fonts, one of them is yours"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is where it gets fun. The extension ships with *246 FIGlet fonts*, so "
"you are never stuck with one look.\n"
"Want something clean and readable? Reach for `standard`, `slant` or `big`. "
"Want to make a statement? `doom`,\n"
"`colossal` and `3d_diagonal` are waiting. There is everything from tidy and "
"corporate to gloriously,\n"
"unapologetically over-the-top -- the same word rendered in `standard`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "...becomes this in `doom`, just by changing one property:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The full catalogue, with author credits, is in the\n"
"https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-banner/blob/main/FIGLET-FONTS."
"md[`FIGLET-FONTS.md`] file in the\n"
"repository."
msgstr ""

msgid "A playground in the Dev UI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Trawling 246 fonts sounds like a chore -- so it is not one. In dev mode the "
"extension adds a *Quarkus Banner*\n"
"card to the http://localhost:8080/q/dev-ui/[Quarkus Dev UI] with a *Preview* "
"page built for exactly this."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Type any text, pick any font from the list, toggle the _Powered by Quarkus_ "
"tagline, and the rendered banner\n"
"updates live in front of you -- no restart, no HTTP request, no rebuild. "
"When you find the one, a *Print to log*\n"
"button drops it straight into your application console so you can see it in "
"context. Cycling through fonts until\n"
"one clicks becomes the genuinely fun five minutes it should be."
msgstr ""

msgid "The good bits"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The banner is rendered at *build time*, so there is zero runtime cost -- it "
"is baked in, not computed on every\n"
"start-up."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It slots in exactly where Quarkus' own banner goes, honouring your console "
"colours and format, and it shows up\n"
"when you run your tests too."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nothing to disable and nothing to break: if you turn it off, or the text "
"will not render, you simply get the\n"
"default Quarkus banner back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Everything else -- the config options and dev-mode tips -- lives in the\n"
"https://docs.quarkiverse.io/quarkus-banner/dev/[extension documentation]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Give it a go"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus Banner is deliberately tiny. It does one thing: it makes your "
"application instantly recognisable, and it\n"
"makes start-up a little more fun."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"I would love to hear what you think -- which fonts you land on, where it is "
"useful, and especially what you would\n"
"like it to do next. Drop your thoughts, ideas and feature requests on the\n"
"https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-banner[GitHub repository]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Happy bannering!"
msgstr ""
